// Dying in Survival is recoverable. A mole that drowns in a flooded passage leaves its pack on the last dry
// ground it stood on (here the floor by the hole it dropped into), not under the water where the next trip
// would drown it again; the log says why it died and where the pack is. Back in the burrow its stores give
// a meal and fill the headlamp (no items: the pack is still lost until fetched), so there is time and light
// to go back. Walking over the pack takes it back. (The passage roof is bedrock so it can't cave in.)
map
BBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
#......................................#
#......................................#
#......................................#
#.....@................................#
##########wwwwwBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBB
##########wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww#######
##########wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww#######
########################################
end
mode survival
set 1 hunger 50
set 1 oil 30
// walk right: into the flooded hole, wedged under the passage roof (too low to pass) until the breath runs out
hold 5-200 right
expect 1700 deaths >= 1
expect 1700 log:drowned == 1
expect 1700 log:on_dry_ground_near_where_you_fell == 1
// the pack lies on the floor by the hole (tile row 0), not down in the passage (rows 1-3)
expect 1700 items:Pickaxe == 1
expect 1700 ix:Pickaxe < 6
expect 1700 iy:Pickaxe < 0.6
// back in the burrow: fed and lit from its stores, but the pack isn't
expect 1700 hunger > 95
expect 1700 oil > 170
expect 1700 inv:Pickaxe == 0
expect 1700 log:its_stores_give_you_a_meal == 1
// fetch it: a few steps right
hold 1705-1730 right
expect 1760 inv:Pickaxe == 1
expect 1760 inv:Grub == 3
